# GDR cards: rooms, scenes and game flow for the Godot rebuild (planner: Sonnet 5.5, 14 Oct 2026).
# Contracts: docs/GODOT_PLANNER_BRIEF.md. Every card is one small script (or one scene + its builder) with a headless test.
# Key conventions invented HERE (other planners must match, see the last reply of the planner):
#   RoomHotspot (tap rule control), RoomButton, RoomMenu, RoomBase (layers Background/Props/Characters/Lights/Front + Ui + Hotspots),
#   FakeGame (test double for the Game autoload), Flow (script on main.tscn), Save and SettingsStore (static classes), Transitions node.
MODE = "godot"

JS = "/Users/leelangley/wt/webbwheresmycar/_dev/"
GODOT = "docs/GODOT.md (plan, TV-centred layout, tap rule, determinism) and docs/GODOT_PLANNER_BRIEF.md section SHARED CONTRACTS (Game, Data, Sim*, Core*, tests, tools)"
ZONES = "STAGE ZONES (1280x720): banner y 0..120, tableau y 120..590, HUD strip y 590..720. In main.tscn the Hud and Banner are separate nodes; a room keeps every tappable rect inside y 120..590 (the TV may overlap the zones a little)."
TESTS = "Tests: `godot/tests/test_<name>.gd` starts with `extends \"res://tests/harness.gd\"`; every method named `test_*` runs; helpers `ok(cond, msg)`, `eq(a, b, msg)`, `near(a, b, eps, msg)`. Run one file with `sh tools/godot/gtest.sh test_<name>` (last line `GDTEST OK`)."
HYGIENE = "Test hygiene: get the tree with `var tree := Engine.get_main_loop() as SceneTree`; add a node with `tree.root.add_child(n)` when its `_ready` must run; at the end of each test `tree.root.remove_child(n)` (if added) and `n.free()`. Nodes made with `.new()` and never added can simply be `free()`d."
FAKE = "godot/tests/fake_game.gd (GDR19): `FakeGame.new()` is a stand-in for the Game autoload with the same surface: `state` (Dictionary, JS key names such as day, cash, cars[].modelId), `act(action, params) -> Dictionary` (records `[action, params]` in `calls` and returns `result`, default `{\"ok\": true, \"msg\": \"\"}`), and signals `changed`, `toast_requested(text)`, `day_advanced`, `game_over`. A room gets it with `room.game = FakeGame.new()` BEFORE it is added to the tree."
ROOMAPI = "godot/rooms/room_base.gd (GDR19, class `RoomBase extends Control`): `LAYER_NAMES`, `build_layers()`, `layer(name)`, `placeholder(name)`, `set_plate(layer, tex, pos)`, `add_hotspot(id, rect)`, `hotspots`, `game` + `get_game()`, signals `request_scene(scene_id: StringName, params: Dictionary)`, `chatter(text)`, `toast(text)`, statics `add_box`, `add_panel`, `add_label`, `pixel_font`. Rooms are built IN CODE in `_ready` (the .tscn is only a root Control with the script), so every node name in a card is an exact contract for the art cards (GDA) and the tests."
ACT = "Action names and parameters this card assumes in `Game.act` (the GDS planner must provide them): `advance` (the kettle; one day passes), `service_car {carId, kind: 'quick'|'full'}`, `fix_fault {carId}`, `restore_car {carId}`, `sell_to_dealer {carId}`, `return_rental {carId}`, `consign_car {carId, reserve}`, `unconsign {carId}`, `attend_auction {}`, `reveal_stat {lotId, stat}`, `place_bid {lotId, steps}`. Every result is a Dictionary with `ok` (bool) and `msg` (String), exactly as src/sim/actions.js. Parameter keys are camelCase like the state keys."
SHOT = "Screenshot step: run `sh tools/godot/gshot.sh {scene} /tmp/{name}.png 8`, then LOOK at the PNG with the Read tool and describe it in your final reply (what is where, anything overlapping, anything off screen). If the screenshot step fails because the card it needs is not merged, say so, do not fake it."

